==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{term|per||through|lang=la}} + {{term|sonō||make a noise, sound, resound|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈper.so.noː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|personō|personāre|personuī|personātum|conj=1}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=la}} I [[sound]] through and through, [[resound]], [[ring]].
#* '''1832''', [[w:Pope Gregory XVI|Gregory XVI]], ''[[:w:Mirari Vos|Mirari Vos]]''
#*: '''Personant''' horrendum in modum academiae ac gymnasia novis opinionum monstris, quibus non occulte amplius et cuniculis petitur catholica fides […]
# {{context|intransitive|lang=la}} I make a sound on a [[musical instrument]], [[play]], sound.
# {{context|transitive|lang=la}} I [[fill]] with sound, make resound.
# {{context|transitive|rare|lang=la}} I [[cry out]], [[call]] aloud.

====Inflection====
* Note that [[personavit|personāvit]] is an alternative form for the third-person singular perfect active indicative [[personuit]].
{{la-conj-1st|person|personu|personāt}}

